{% if agenda.earlier | length %}
<details class="agenda-earlier">
  <summary>Earlier meetings ({{ agenda.earlier | length }})</summary>
  <ul class="agenda-list">
  {% for m in agenda.earlier %}
    <li class="agenda-row">
      <p class="agenda-when">{{ m.display }}</p>
      <p class="agenda-what">
        {% if m.url %}<a href="{{ m.url }}">{{ m.committee }}</a>
        {% else %}{{ m.committee }}{% endif %}
      </p>
      <p class="agenda-detail">{{ m.hits }} mention{% if m.hits != 1 %}s{% endif %}
      in the papers{% if m.read %}, counted by this site from the pack{% endif %}</p>
    </li>
  {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</details>
{% endif %}

<details class="agenda-how">
  <summary>How this page is made</summary>
  <p>Three things are put together. North Ayrshire publishes a calendar of its
  committee meetings months in advance, which is where the dates come from. It
  runs a search across its own committee documents, which is where the older
  mention counts come from. And because that search can take a fortnight or
  more to index new papers, this site now reads the agenda pack for each
  meeting ahead itself and counts the word “Largs” in it — the same measure
  the council's search reports, checked against it. A row says when the count
  is ours. Only the number is kept: nothing from inside a pack is copied here.
  Nothing on this page is written by hand, and nothing is interpreted.</p>
  <p>A mention can be substantial or trivial. A town name in a list of
  settlements counts the same as a decision about the town, and there is no way
  to tell which is which without opening the paper. That is why this page points
  rather than summarises.</p>
  <p>Papers are normally published at least three days before a meeting, so a
  meeting listed without papers is not being ignored — the documents simply do
  not exist yet. Minutes follow afterwards.</p>
  {% if agenda.counts %}
  <p class="agenda-meta">{{ agenda.counts.meetings }} meetings known,
  {{ agenda.counts.mentioned }} with papers mentioning Largs{% if agenda.cutoff %},
  back to {{ agenda.cutoff }}{% endif %}.</p>
  {% endif %}
</details>

<p class="agenda-note">Two different councils. This page is North Ayrshire
Council, the local authority, which runs the schools, the roads and the bins.
What Largs Community Council discussed, and what it is still pursuing, is in
<a href="/council/">Largs Community Council</a>.</p>

{% endif %}
